{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c519","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a073c4-c6ec-7382-9783-190de4ee11a6"},"sequence":231,"recorded_at":1780531400000457,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"7f2c8277-7d4a-4f8c-bde1-d0d1e6d97d2b"},"task_id":"7f2c8277-7d4a-4f8c-bde1-d0d1e6d97d2b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"7f2c8277-7d4a-4f8c-bde1-d0d1e6d97d2b","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(3486 line(s) above)\n3487|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3488|\n3489|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3490|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3491|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3492|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3493|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3494|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3495|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3496|\n3497|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3498|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3499|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3500|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3501|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3502|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3503|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3504|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3505|\n3506|The closed operation registry is:\n3507|\n3508|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3509|| --- | --- |\n3510|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3511|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3512|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3513|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3514|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3515|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3516|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3517|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3518|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3519|\n3520|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3521|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3522|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3523|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3524|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3525|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3526|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3527|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3528|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3529|every candidate object.\n3530|\n3531|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n3532|<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\n3533|<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\n3534|Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n3535|embedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\n3536|\n3537|- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\n3538|  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3539|  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n3540|  <code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3541|  <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>, <code>request_digest:digest</code>,\n3542|  and <code>extensions</code>. The host constructs it from the verified\n3543|  candidate. <code>request_digest</code> is the digest of the JCS request body\n3544|  with only that member omitted. Every success echoes the context byte-for-byte.\n3545|- <code>ReadAuthority</code> contains exactly <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3546|  <code>purpose:source_native|target_staged|target_live</code>,\n3547|  <code>root_handle_names:sorted unique string[1..128][1..128]</code>,\n3548|  <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Handle names\n3549|  identify host-opened descriptors or handles delivered out of band; they are\n3550|  never paths.\n3551|- <code>ObjectAuthority</code> contains exactly\n3552|  <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3553|  <code>purpose:capture_plan|raw_source|canonical_source|projection_plan|projected_target|read_back_evidence</code>,\n3554|  <code>mode:read|fresh_sink</code>, <code>max_objects:uint53</code>,\n3555|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3556|  <code>fresh_sink</code> requires an empty host-created sink and both limits\n3557|  greater than zero. <code>read</code> exposes only request-named objects.\n3558|- <code>SourceSelector</code> contains exactly\n3559|  <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n3560|  <code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and\n3561|  <code>opaque_source_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>; exactly one is non-null.\n3562|- <code>AdapterFinding</code> contains exactly\n3563|  <code>severity:info|warning|error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n3564|  <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3565|  <code>remediation:string[1..4096]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3566|- <code>ResourceLimits</code> contains exactly\n3567|  <code>max_objects:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3568|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3569|  <code>max_single_object_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3570|  <code>max_events:uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n3571|  <code>max_target_resources:uint53[0..65536]</code>. Each per-item maximum is\n3572|  no greater than <code>max_total_bytes</code>.\n3573|- <code>CapturePlanItem</code> contains exactly\n3574|  <code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n3575|  <code>class:capture-class</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n3576|  <code>required:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3577|\n3578|The exact request and success <code>body</code> registry is:\n3579|\n3580|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3581|| --- | --- | --- |\n3582|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 |\n3583|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\n3584|| <code>discover</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,workspace_filter:UUIDv7\\|null,limit:uint53[1..65536],cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,sources:CloneSourceSummary[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code>; sorted by logical workspace/native Session ID; <code>partial=false</code> iff <code>next_cursor</code> is null |\n3585|| <code>inspect</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source:CloneSourceSummary,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],environment:EnvironmentTuple,ambiguities:AdapterFinding[0..1024],extensions}</code>; zero ambiguities are required before capture |\n3586|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,expected_source_store_generation:string[1..512],allow_provider_quiescence:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,proof:StableSnapshotProof,provider_quiescence_requested:boolean,provider_quiescence_observed:boolean,extensions}</code>; provider quiescence requires both booleans true and separately verified Provider <code>quiesce</code> evidence |\n3587|| <code>capture-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,max_items:uint53[1..65536],max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_plan_candidate_id:digest,candidate_count:uint53[0..65536],excluded_classes:sorted unique capture-class[0..9],capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh <code>capture_plan</code> sink containing exactly sorted unique <code>CapturePlanItem[0..65536]</code>, and the two candidate digests are equal after core rehash |\n3588|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_authority:ReadAuthority,sink:ObjectAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_plan_digest:digest,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_result_candidate_id:digest,source_raw_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,item_count:uint53[0..65536],pre_capture_digest:digest,post_capture_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh raw sink, exact plan-key reconciliation, and an exact included-object closure |\n3589|| <code>normalize</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,raw_objects:ObjectAuthority,canonical_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_candidate_id:digest,canonical_event_candidate_ids:digest[0..65536],raw_reference_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],extensions}</code>; all candidates resolve inside the fresh canonical sink and all raw references are in Capture Manifest closure |\n3590|| <code>projection-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,canonical_event_ids:digest[0..65536],source_objects:ObjectAuthority,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,target_environment:EnvironmentTuple,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],fidelity_profile:strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only,required_dispositions:closed-map(event-or-artifact-class,sorted-unique-fidelity-disposition[1..7]),forbid_reasons:sorted-unique-string[1..128][0..128],resource_limits:ResourceLimits,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_candidate_id:digest,required_source_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],predicted_counts:FidelityCounts,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code>; <code>archive_only</code> is forbidden and every canonical item has one disposition |\n3591|| <code>project</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,source_objects:ObjectAuthority,target_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,created_resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][0..65536],actual_counts:FidelityCounts,extensions}</code>; fresh target sink and exact plan/manifest/resource-key reconciliation |\n3592|| <code>read-back</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_id:digest,evidence_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,observed_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple,parsed_event_count:uint53,parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024],workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding,structural_digest:digest,read_back_evidence_manifest_candidate_id:digest,extensions}</code>; staged/live mode is fixed by authority and cannot be relabeled |\n3593|| <code>validate</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,projection_plan_id:digest\\|null,projected_object_manifest_id:digest\\|null,read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest\\|null,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,valid:boolean,structural_valid:boolean,semantic_marker_valid:boolean,identity_valid:boolean\\|null,workspace_binding_valid:boolean\\|null,resume_surface_valid:boolean\\|null,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],evidence_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; archive requires all four target members null, staged/live require them non-null, and <code>valid=true</code> requires every applicable check true and no error finding |\n3594|| <code>resume-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,target_checkpoint_id:digest\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,argv:string[1..4096][1..128],cwd_relative:string[1..4096],environment_names:sorted unique string[1..256][0..128],opens_existing_identity:true,extensions}</code>; argv contains no secret, names the trusted CLI family, and contains the explicit identity exactly once |\n3595|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,tuple_registry_digest:digest,refresh_requested:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,registry_sequence:uint53,registry_entry_status:accepted\\|revoked\\|absent,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],healthy:boolean,extensions}</code>; healthy requires an accepted exact binding and every required capability |\n3596|\n3597|Candidate objects are addressed only by their exact\n3598|<code>*_candidate_id</code> in the request's fresh sink. The core retrieves,\n3599|validates, rehashes, and seals them. A partial, malformed, over-limit, escaped,\n3600|or authority-unresolvable result is an error, never an empty or absent result\n3601|and never fallback permission.\n3602|\n3603|Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly:\n3604|\n3605|| Member | Type and constraint |\n3606|| --- | --- |\n3607|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n3608|| <code>provider_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>; equal to Provider Manifest and discovered candidate ID |\n3609|| <code>environment_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}</code>; one semantic native environment |\n3610|| <code>display_name</code> / <code>adapter_version</code> | UTF-8 string[1..128] / SemVer |\n3611|| <code>environment_version_range</code> | Non-empty constraint string[1..256] |\n3612|| <code>platforms</code> | Sorted unique non-empty subset of <code>linux&#124;macos&#124;windows&#124;wsl2</code> |\n3613|| <code>operations</code> / <code>capability_names</code> | Complete ordered registries in this section, no omissions or duplicates |\n3614|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; cannot add operations, capabilities, or trust facts |\n3615|\n3616|Its host-computed JCS SHA-256 is\n3617|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest</code> and is not embedded.\n3618|\n3619|Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly\n3620|<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-probe</code>,\n3621|<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>, <code>provider_id</code>,\n3622|<code>adapter_manifest_digest</code>, <code>adapter_version</code>,\n3623|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>, <code>capabilities</code>,\n3624|<code>warnings:sorted unique string[0..2048][0..1024]</code>, and\n3625|<code>extensions</code>. Provider ID, manifest digest, and adapter version equal\n3626|the verified Manifest and host values. Environment Tuple contains exactly\n3627|<code>environment_id</code>, <code>environment_version</code>,\n3628|<code>platform=linux|macos|windows|wsl2</code>,\n3629|<code>architecture=amd64|arm64</code>,\n3630|<code>store_schema_fingerprint</code>, and <code>adapter_version</code>; it\n3631|never contains executable provenance.\n3632|\n3633|The exact capability names are <code>native_discovery</code>,\n3634|<code>stable_snapshot</code>, <code>raw_capture</code>,\n3635|<code>canonical_read</code>, <code>canonical_write</code>,\n3636|<code>native_read_back</code>, <code>native_resume_plan</code>,\n3637|<code>official_import</code>, <code>same_environment_lossless_clone</code>,\n3638|<code>tool_history</code>, <code>usage_history</code>,\n3639|<code>compaction_history</code>, <code>subagent_graph</code>,\n3640|<code>opaque_reasoning_roundtrip</code>, and <code>workspace_binding</code>.\n3641|Each value contains exactly status, enabled, evidence, and detail; only\n3642|<code>status=available</code> permits <code>enabled=true</code>.\n3643|\n3644|Each capability value contains exactly\n3645|<code>status:available|conditional|unsupported|unknown</code>,\n3646|<code>enabled:boolean</code>,\n3647|<code>evidence:documented|probed|accepted_test|provider_contract|inferred|acceptance_required|none</code>,\n3648|and <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code>. Missing, extra, duplicated, malformed,\n3649|or contradictory facts invalidate the whole Probe and never mean unsupported.\n3650|\n3651|For source and target, the host seals a closed\n3652|<code>SessionAdapterExecutionBinding</code> containing exactly\n3653|<code>role:source|target</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3654|<code>candidate_kind:builtin|external</code>,\n3655|<code>canonical_executable_path:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3656|<code>owner_identity:string[1..512]</code>,\n3657|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3658|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3659|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3660|<code>verified_at:timestamp</code>. Before every call and\n3661|target mutation, these facts MUST equal freshly read trusted-candidate facts\n3662|and the Journal binding. A failed/partial read is an integrity failure; no\n3663|self-claim or publisher claim establishes trust.\n3664|\n3665|A target write requires available canonical-write or official-import,\n3666|native-read-back, native-resume-plan, workspace-binding, Provider\n3667|portable-store and native-resume capabilities; exact execution bindings;\n3668|accepted non-revoked signed source/target tuple entries; and current fixture\n3669|plus bounded native-resume smoke evidence. <code>--force</code>, experimental\n3670|profiles, and environment-name-only matches cannot bypass these gates. Unknown\n3671|sources may be archived only after safe byte enumeration; unknown targets never\n3672|write.\n3673|\n3674|### 7.9 Companion Directory Node protocol\n3675|\n3676|Directory Node protocol <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-directory-node</code>\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c51b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a073c4-c6ec-7382-9783-190de4ee11a6"},"sequence":232,"recorded_at":1780531400000459,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"7f2c8277-7d4a-4f8c-bde1-d0d1e6d97d2b"},"task_id":"7f2c8277-7d4a-4f8c-bde1-d0d1e6d97d2b","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"7f2c8277-7d4a-4f8c-bde1-d0d1e6d97d2b"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c51d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a073c4-c6ec-7382-9783-190de4ee11a6"},"sequence":233,"recorded_at":1780531400000461,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09"},"call_id":"call_01a073c5493e7510820e802df538ccf0","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(3486 line(s) above)\n3487|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3488|\n3489|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3490|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3491|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3492|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3493|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3494|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3495|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3496|\n3497|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3498|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3499|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3500|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3501|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3502|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3503|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3504|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3505|\n3506|The closed operation registry is:\n3507|\n3508|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3509|| --- | --- |\n3510|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3511|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3512|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3513|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3514|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3515|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3516|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3517|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3518|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3519|\n3520|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3521|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3522|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3523|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3524|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3525|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3526|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3527|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3528|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3529|every candidate object.\n3530|\n3531|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n3532|<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\n3533|<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\n3534|Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n3535|embedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\n3536|\n3537|- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\n3538|  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3539|  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n3540|  <code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3541|  <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>, <code>request_digest:digest</code>,\n3542|  and <code>extensions</code>. The host constructs it from the verified\n3543|  candidate. <code>request_digest</code> is the digest of the JCS request body\n3544|  with only that member omitted. Every success echoes the context byte-for-byte.\n3545|- <code>ReadAuthority</code> contains exactly <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3546|  <code>purpose:source_native|target_staged|target_live</code>,\n3547|  <code>root_handle_names:sorted unique string[1..128][1..128]</code>,\n3548|  <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Handle names\n3549|  identify host-opened descriptors or handles delivered out of band; they are\n3550|  never paths.\n3551|- <code>ObjectAuthority</code> contains exactly\n3552|  <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3553|  <code>purpose:capture_plan|raw_source|canonical_source|projection_plan|projected_target|read_back_evidence</code>,\n3554|  <code>mode:read|fresh_sink</code>, <code>max_objects:uint53</code>,\n3555|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3556|  <code>fresh_sink</code> requires an empty host-created sink and both limits\n3557|  greater than zero. <code>read</code> exposes only request-named objects.\n3558|- <code>SourceSelector</code> contains exactly\n3559|  <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n3560|  <code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and\n3561|  <code>opaque_source_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>; exactly one is non-null.\n3562|- <code>AdapterFinding</code> contains exactly\n3563|  <code>severity:info|warning|error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n3564|  <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3565|  <code>remediation:string[1..4096]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3566|- <code>ResourceLimits</code> contains exactly\n3567|  <code>max_objects:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3568|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3569|  <code>max_single_object_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3570|  <code>max_events:uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n3571|  <code>max_target_resources:uint53[0..65536]</code>. Each per-item maximum is\n3572|  no greater than <code>max_total_bytes</code>.\n3573|- <code>CapturePlanItem</code> contains exactly\n3574|  <code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n3575|  <code>class:capture-class</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n3576|  <code>required:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3577|\n3578|The exact request and success <code>body</code> registry is:\n3579|\n3580|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3581|| --- | --- | --- |\n3582|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 |\n3583|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\n3584|| <code>discover</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,workspace_filter:UUIDv7\\|null,limit:uint53[1..65536],cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,sources:CloneSourceSummary[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code>; sorted by logical workspace/native Session ID; <code>partial=false</code> iff <code>next_cursor</code> is null |\n3585|| <code>inspect</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source:CloneSourceSummary,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],environment:EnvironmentTuple,ambiguities:AdapterFinding[0..1024],extensions}</code>; zero ambiguities are required before capture |\n3586|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,expected_source_store_generation:string[1..512],allow_provider_quiescence:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,proof:StableSnapshotProof,provider_quiescence_requested:boolean,provider_quiescence_observed:boolean,extensions}</code>; provider quiescence requires both booleans true and separately verified Provider <code>quiesce</code> evidence |\n3587|| <code>capture-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,max_items:uint53[1..65536],max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_plan_candidate_id:digest,candidate_count:uint53[0..65536],excluded_classes:sorted unique capture-class[0..9],capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh <code>capture_plan</code> sink containing exactly sorted unique <code>CapturePlanItem[0..65536]</code>, and the two candidate digests are equal after core rehash |\n3588|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_authority:ReadAuthority,sink:ObjectAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_plan_digest:digest,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_result_candidate_id:digest,source_raw_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,item_count:uint53[0..65536],pre_capture_digest:digest,post_capture_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh raw sink, exact plan-key reconciliation, and an exact included-object closure |\n3589|| <code>normalize</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,raw_objects:ObjectAuthority,canonical_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_candidate_id:digest,canonical_event_candidate_ids:digest[0..65536],raw_reference_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],extensions}</code>; all candidates resolve inside the fresh canonical sink and all raw references are in Capture Manifest closure |\n3590|| <code>projection-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,canonical_event_ids:digest[0..65536],source_objects:ObjectAuthority,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,target_environment:EnvironmentTuple,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],fidelity_profile:strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only,required_dispositions:closed-map(event-or-artifact-class,sorted-unique-fidelity-disposition[1..7]),forbid_reasons:sorted-unique-string[1..128][0..128],resource_limits:ResourceLimits,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_candidate_id:digest,required_source_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],predicted_counts:FidelityCounts,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code>; <code>archive_only</code> is forbidden and every canonical item has one disposition |\n3591|| <code>project</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,source_objects:ObjectAuthority,target_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,created_resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][0..65536],actual_counts:FidelityCounts,extensions}</code>; fresh target sink and exact plan/manifest/resource-key reconciliation |\n3592|| <code>read-back</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_id:digest,evidence_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,observed_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple,parsed_event_count:uint53,parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024],workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding,structural_digest:digest,read_back_evidence_manifest_candidate_id:digest,extensions}</code>; staged/live mode is fixed by authority and cannot be relabeled |\n3593|| <code>validate</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,projection_plan_id:digest\\|null,projected_object_manifest_id:digest\\|null,read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest\\|null,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,valid:boolean,structural_valid:boolean,semantic_marker_valid:boolean,identity_valid:boolean\\|null,workspace_binding_valid:boolean\\|null,resume_surface_valid:boolean\\|null,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],evidence_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; archive requires all four target members null, staged/live require them non-null, and <code>valid=true</code> requires every applicable check true and no error finding |\n3594|| <code>resume-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,target_checkpoint_id:digest\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,argv:string[1..4096][1..128],cwd_relative:string[1..4096],environment_names:sorted unique string[1..256][0..128],opens_existing_identity:true,extensions}</code>; argv contains no secret, names the trusted CLI family, and contains the explicit identity exactly once |\n3595|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,tuple_registry_digest:digest,refresh_requested:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,registry_sequence:uint53,registry_entry_status:accepted\\|revoked\\|absent,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],healthy:boolean,extensions}</code>; healthy requires an accepted exact binding and every required capability |\n3596|\n3597|Candidate objects are addressed only by their exact\n3598|<code>*_candidate_id</code> in the request's fresh sink. The core retrieves,\n3599|validates, rehashes, and seals them. A partial, malformed, over-limit, escaped,\n3600|or authority-unresolvable result is an error, never an empty or absent result\n3601|and never fallback permission.\n3602|\n3603|Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly:\n3604|\n3605|| Member | Type and constraint |\n3606|| --- | --- |\n3607|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n3608|| <code>provider_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>; equal to Provider Manifest and discovered candidate ID |\n3609|| <code>environment_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}</code>; one semantic native environment |\n3610|| <code>display_name</code> / <code>adapter_version</code> | UTF-8 string[1..128] / SemVer |\n3611|| <code>environment_version_range</code> | Non-empty constraint string[1..256] |\n3612|| <code>platforms</code> | Sorted unique non-empty subset of <code>linux&#124;macos&#124;windows&#124;wsl2</code> |\n3613|| <code>operations</code> / <code>capability_names</code> | Complete ordered registries in this section, no omissions or duplicates |\n3614|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; cannot add operations, capabilities, or trust facts |\n3615|\n3616|Its host-computed JCS SHA-256 is\n3617|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest</code> and is not embedded.\n3618|\n3619|Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly\n3620|<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-probe</code>,\n3621|<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>, <code>provider_id</code>,\n3622|<code>adapter_manifest_digest</code>, <code>adapter_version</code>,\n3623|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>, <code>capabilities</code>,\n3624|<code>warnings:sorted unique string[0..2048][0..1024]</code>, and\n3625|<code>extensions</code>. Provider ID, manifest digest, and adapter version equal\n3626|the verified Manifest and host values. Environment Tuple contains exactly\n3627|<code>environment_id</code>, <code>environment_version</code>,\n3628|<code>platform=linux|macos|windows|wsl2</code>,\n3629|<code>architecture=amd64|arm64</code>,\n3630|<code>store_schema_fingerprint</code>, and <code>adapter_version</code>; it\n3631|never contains executable provenance.\n3632|\n3633|The exact capability names are <code>native_discovery</code>,\n3634|<code>stable_snapshot</code>, <code>raw_capture</code>,\n3635|<code>canonical_read</code>, <code>canonical_write</code>,\n3636|<code>native_read_back</code>, <code>native_resume_plan</code>,\n3637|<code>official_import</code>, <code>same_environment_lossless_clone</code>,\n3638|<code>tool_history</code>, <code>usage_history</code>,\n3639|<code>compaction_history</code>, <code>subagent_graph</code>,\n3640|<code>opaque_reasoning_roundtrip</code>, and <code>workspace_binding</code>.\n3641|Each value contains exactly status, enabled, evidence, and detail; only\n3642|<code>status=available</code> permits <code>enabled=true</code>.\n3643|\n3644|Each capability value contains exactly\n3645|<code>status:available|conditional|unsupported|unknown</code>,\n3646|<code>enabled:boolean</code>,\n3647|<code>evidence:documented|probed|accepted_test|provider_contract|inferred|acceptance_required|none</code>,\n3648|and <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code>. Missing, extra, duplicated, malformed,\n3649|or contradictory facts invalidate the whole Probe and never mean unsupported.\n3650|\n3651|For source and target, the host seals a closed\n3652|<code>SessionAdapterExecutionBinding</code> containing exactly\n3653|<code>role:source|target</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3654|<code>candidate_kind:builtin|external</code>,\n3655|<code>canonical_executable_path:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3656|<code>owner_identity:string[1..512]</code>,\n3657|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3658|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3659|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3660|<code>verified_at:timestamp</code>. Before every call and\n3661|target mutation, these facts MUST equal freshly read trusted-candidate facts\n3662|and the Journal binding. A failed/partial read is an integrity failure; no\n3663|self-claim or publisher claim establishes trust.\n3664|\n3665|A target write requires available canonical-write or official-import,\n3666|native-read-back, native-resume-plan, workspace-binding, Provider\n3667|portable-store and native-resume capabilities; exact execution bindings;\n3668|accepted non-revoked signed source/target tuple entries; and current fixture\n3669|plus bounded native-resume smoke evidence. <code>--force</code>, experimental\n3670|profiles, and environment-name-only matches cannot bypass these gates. Unknown\n3671|sources may be archived only after safe byte enumeration; unknown targets never\n3672|write.\n3673|\n3674|### 7.9 Companion Directory Node protocol\n3675|\n3676|Directory Node protocol <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-directory-node</code>\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
