{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c697","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a073c4-c6ec-7382-9783-190de4ee11a6"},"sequence":422,"recorded_at":1780531400000839,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09"},"call_id":"call_01a073c5aba87c2395dc083b58187951","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(3673 line(s) above)\n3674|### 7.9 Companion Directory Node protocol\n3675|\n3676|Directory Node protocol <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-directory-node</code>\n3677|<code>2.0.0</code> is the current separately negotiated, read-mostly façade\n3678|backed by the same per-environment implementation as Provider 2 and Session\n3679|Adapter 1. Directory Node protocol <code>1.0.0</code> remains an immutable\n3680|legacy wire contract. Neither major adds operations to Provider 2, executes\n3681|Continuation Plans, or transports transcript/workspace bytes.\n3682|\n3683|The exact major bindings are closed:\n3684|\n3685|| Protocol | Request | Response | Manifest | <code>probe.platform</code> vocabulary |\n3686|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3687|| <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>darwin\\|linux\\|windows</code> |\n3688|| <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows</code> |\n3689|\n3690|A v1 <code>darwin</code> request denotes the macOS host class defined by that\n3691|published major, but <code>darwin</code> is not a valid v2 wire value and never\n3692|appears in an Environment Observation. A v1 request cannot express WSL2.\n3693|Implementations MUST validate the vocabulary belonging to the negotiated\n3694|major; they MUST NOT relabel a v1 envelope as v2, relabel a v2 envelope as v1,\n3695|or coerce an unknown token across majors. Implementations supporting v2 SHOULD\n3696|serve v1 concurrently for at least one stable specification release. Peers\n3697|choose the highest mutually supported major and fail closed when no major is\n3698|shared.\n3699|\n3700|A fresh adapter invocation has no trusted manifest from which to discover the\n3701|peer's supported majors. The caller MUST therefore enumerate its locally\n3702|supported Directory Node majors in strictly descending numeric order and make\n3703|one <code>manifest</code> request for the highest not yet attempted major. Each\n3704|attempt MUST launch a fresh process; a process that returned or failed an\n3705|attempt is terminated and reaped and MUST NOT be reused for a lower major. The\n3706|request binds <code>protocol_version</code> and request\n3707|<code>schema_version</code> to the exact attempted <code>N.0.0</code> version and\n3708|uses an empty body.\n3709|\n3710|There is exactly one downgrade trigger. The attempted process MUST return one\n3711|well-framed Directory Node failure response whose <code>protocol</code>,\n3712|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, and\n3713|<code>operation=manifest</code> exactly echo the request and whose response\n3714|<code>schema_version</code> is the bound <code>1.0.0</code>, whose Structured\n3715|Error 1.2 has\n3716|<code>code=incompatible_protocol</code>, <code>exit_code=6</code>, and\n3717|<code>retryable=false</code>, and then exit with status 6. Only that complete\n3718|response-plus-exit tuple authorizes the caller to launch a fresh process for\n3719|the next lower locally supported major. The response is negotiation evidence,\n3720|not trusted manifest data and not an ordinary retryable operation failure.\n3721|\n3722|Success requires one well-framed success response with every echo exact, a\n3723|complete schema-valid manifest whose <code>supported_protocol_versions</code>\n3724|contains the exact selected version, and process exit 0. A wrong or missing\n3725|echo, malformed/partial/extra frame, invalid UTF-8/JSON/schema, timeout,\n3726|signal, nonmatching exit status, authentication/allowlist failure, integrity\n3727|failure, or any error other than the exact downgrade tuple is terminal and\n3728|MUST NOT cause a lower-major attempt. The caller MUST NOT reinterpret a frame,\n3729|manifest, platform token, request body, or error from one major as another.\n3730|If every locally supported major returns the exact downgrade tuple, the caller\n3731|terminates with its own Structured Error 1.2\n3732|<code>incompatible_protocol</code>, exit 6, and no trusted manifest or partial\n3733|result. These rules select v2 directly, permit v2-to-v1 fallback, support a\n3734|v1-only caller/peer, and terminate deterministically when no major is common.\n3735|\n3736|Transport is one request and one response as line-delimited JSON over\n3737|authenticated local stdio or allowlisted AX SSH. One line is at most 8 MiB.\n3738|The request envelope contains exactly <code>schema</code>,\n3739|<code>schema_version</code>, <code>protocol</code>,\n3740|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3741|<code>operation</code>, <code>deadline_ms:uint53[1..3600000]</code>, and the\n3742|closed operation <code>body</code>. The response echoes protocol/version,\n3743|request/operation. A success response contains exactly the common envelope\n3744|members, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>, with no <code>error</code>\n3745|member. A failure response contains exactly the common envelope members,\n3746|<code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.2.0 in <code>error</code>, with no\n3747|<code>body</code> member. Unknown fields, both or neither branch members, invalid\n3748|UTF-8/JSON, multiple frames, wrong echo, oversize, timeout, or exit without one\n3749|valid response fail with no partial trusted data. Stdout is protocol-only;\n3750|redacted diagnostics use stderr.\n3751|\n3752|The Directory Node Manifest contains exactly schema/version,\n3753|<code>node_id:string[1..128]</code>, <code>node_version:semver</code>,\n3754|<code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3755|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3756|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3757|<code>supported_protocol_versions:sorted unique SemVer[1..16]</code>,\n3758|<code>operations:sorted unique DirectoryNodeOperation[11]</code>,\n3759|<code>schemas:sorted unique ContractAssertion[15..64]</code>,\n3760|<code>environment_tuple_registry_id:digest</code>,\n3761|<code>capabilities:map(directory-capability,CapabilityResult)[8]</code>,\n3762|<code>redaction_policy_ids:sorted unique digest[1..64]</code>,\n3763|<code>enrichment_profile_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256]</code>,\n3764|<code>limits:DirectoryNodeLimits</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. The three\n3765|façade executable/module bindings and tuple declarations MUST agree; a\n3766|contradiction is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\n3767|\n3768|<code>CapabilityResult</code> contains exactly\n3769|<code>status:available|conditional|unavailable|unknown</code>,\n3770|<code>reason_code:string[1..128]|null</code>,\n3771|<code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[0..64]</code>,\n3772|<code>observed_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Available has a\n3773|null reason; every other status requires one. <code>DirectoryNodeLimits</code>\n3774|contains exactly <code>max_frame_bytes:uint53[1..8388608]</code>,\n3775|<code>max_scan_instances:uint53[1..65536]</code>,\n3776|<code>max_inventory_take:uint53[1..1000]</code>,\n3777|<code>max_excerpt_count:uint53[0..20]</code>,\n3778|<code>max_excerpt_bytes:uint53[0..4096]</code>,\n3779|<code>max_enrichment_events:uint53[1..5000]</code>,\n3780|<code>max_enrichment_bytes:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and\n3781|<code>extensions</code>. Both nested objects are closed except for their listed\n3782|reverse-DNS extension maps.\n3783|\n3784|The exact operation registry and bodies are:\n3785|\n3786|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body | Mutation |\n3787|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3788|| <code>manifest</code> | empty object | complete Directory Node Manifest | none |\n3789|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,architecture:amd64\\|arm64,requested_environment_ids:sorted unique environment-id[0..64],requested_capabilities:sorted unique directory-capability[0..8],extensions}</code> | <code>{host_id:UUIDv7,node_build:DirectoryNodeBuild,policy_digest:digest,environments:EnvironmentObservation[0..256],findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code> | none |\n3790|| <code>scan</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,installation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],prior_batch_id:digest|null,cursor:string[1..4096]|null,max_instances:uint53[1..65536],extensions}</code> | <code>{batch:InventoryBatch,environment_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],native_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..4096]|null,extensions}</code> | directory records only |\n3791|| <code>inventory</code> | <code>{installation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],fields:sorted unique observation-field[1..32],after:string[1..4096]|null,take:uint53[1..1000],extensions}</code> | <code>{observations:NativeSessionObservation[0..1000],next_cursor:string[1..4096]|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code> | none |\n3792|| <code>preview</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,expected_head_digest:digest,roles:sorted unique user\\|assistant[1..2],excerpt_count:uint53[0..20],excerpt_bytes:uint53[0..4096],redaction_policy_id:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{host_id:UUIDv7,instance_id:digest,observation_id:digest,head_digest:digest,excerpts:PreviewExcerpt[0..20],truncated:boolean,redaction_summary:RedactionSummary,freshness:DirectoryFreshness,extensions}</code> | none |\n3793|| <code>enrichment-plan</code> | <code>{request:EnrichmentJobRequest,extensions}</code> | <code>{accepted:boolean,expected_input_events:uint53,expected_input_bytes:uint53,expected_model_calls:uint53,disclosure_classes:sorted unique string[0..64],blockers:sorted unique string[0..128],extensions}</code> | none |\n3794|| <code>enrichment-run</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,request:EnrichmentJobRequest,extensions}</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,current_receipt_id:digest,produced_annotation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..16],extensions}</code> | annotation/job records only |\n3795|| <code>enrichment-status</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,extensions}</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,current_receipt_id:digest,receipt_chain_ids:digest[1..4096],produced_annotation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..16],extensions}</code> | none |\n3796|| <code>continuation-inspect</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,expected_head_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{observation_id:digest,head_digest:digest,management_binding:ManagementBinding,safe_boundary_status:proven\\|unproven\\|not_required,runtime_status:RuntimeExpectation,warnings:sorted unique string[0..256],extensions}</code> | none |\n3797|| <code>runtime-observe</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{runtime:RuntimeExpectation,extensions}</code> | none |\n3798|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{installation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256],include_conformance_age:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{healthy:boolean,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],environment_capabilities:map(digest,map(directory-capability,CapabilityResult))[0..256],cloning_contracts:sorted unique ContractAssertion[0..64],extensions}</code> | none |\n3799|\n3800|Each displayed body is closed; its member types, ordering, and limits are the\n3801|registered Section 10.8 schemas and manifest bounds. The <code>probe</code> row\n3802|shown above is the Request 2.0.0 form; Request 1.0.0 differs only in its closed\n3803|legacy platform vocabulary recorded in the major-binding table. The capability\n3804|registry is exactly <code>directory_discovery</code>,\n3805|<code>directory_incremental_scan</code>, <code>directory_head_digest</code>,\n3806|<code>directory_tail_preview</code>, <code>native_title_read</code>,\n3807|<code>native_runtime_observation</code>,\n3808|<code>existing_session_adoption</code>, and <code>native_resume</code>.\n3809|The closed <code>observation-field</code> registry is exactly\n3810|<code>identity</code>, <code>management</code>, <code>head</code>,\n3811|<code>state</code>, <code>workspace</code>, <code>title</code>,\n3812|<code>counts</code>, <code>preview_status</code>, <code>warnings</code>, and\n3813|<code>timestamps</code>. <code>PreviewExcerpt</code> contains exactly\n3814|<code>role:user|assistant</code>, <code>ordinal:uint53</code>,\n3815|<code>text:string[0..4096]</code>, <code>source_event_id:digest</code>,\n3816|<code>truncated:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3817|<code>ManagementBinding</code> contains exactly\n3818|<code>state:managed|unmanaged|conflicted</code>,\n3819|<code>session_id:UUIDv7|null</code>,\n3820|<code>provider_identity_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n3821|<code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n3822|<code>extensions</code>; both IDs and non-empty evidence are required exactly\n3823|for managed, both IDs are null for unmanaged, and conflicted retains all\n3824|evidence without choosing a winner. These nested objects are closed except for\n3825|their listed extension maps. <code>DirectoryNodeBuild</code> contains exactly\n3826|<code>node_id:string[1..128]</code>, <code>node_version:semver</code>,\n3827|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3828|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3829|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3830|<code>extensions</code>; every value equals the current manifest.\n3831|Discovery may degrade for an unknown source tuple only when stable identity and\n3832|bounds remain safe; head/preview/resume/adoption/write/launch fail closed.\n3833|\n3834|<code>scan</code> and <code>enrichment-run</code> use\n3835|<code>(operation,operation_id)</code> idempotency. Repeating the same canonical\n3836|body returns the prior durable result; a changed body is\n3837|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code> without new records. Scan reads only declared\n3838|non-auth roots, publishes observations and its Inventory Batch atomically, and\n3839|never claims that an active prefix is a cloning-safe boundary. Preview requires\n3840|the exact observation/head, defaults to public user/assistant roles, and\n3841|returns bounded redacted terminal-safe text. Raw native IDs and absolute paths\n3842|never leave the source except through an existing AX mutation authority.\n3843|\n3844|## 8. Provider and platform contracts\n3845|\n3846|### 8.1 Matrix notation\n3847|\n3848|Provider and platform matrices use:\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
