{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6db","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a073c4-c6ec-7382-9783-190de4ee11a6"},"sequence":456,"recorded_at":1780531400000907,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"68c52a17-3795-4113-833b-e46726fc4e66"},"task_id":"68c52a17-3795-4113-833b-e46726fc4e66","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"68c52a17-3795-4113-833b-e46726fc4e66","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(9999 line(s) above)\n10000|for clone.committed matching Session Record 2 provenance, committed Provider\n10001|with null rollback token, and newest validated epoch-1 target Checkpoint proving\n10002|the exact unopened identity. Missing/stale evidence is\n10003|<code>invalid_state_transition</code>. Origin/fork cannot use this edge.\n10004|Optional open follows ordinary resume from that exact Checkpoint and Identity.\n10005|\n10006|Supported Environment Tuple Registry 1.0.0 contains schema/version/digest,\n10007|strictly increasing sequence, AX release, validity interval, sorted entries,\n10008|and extensions. Each key combines direction, exact six-member tuple, provider,\n10009|candidate kind, executable SHA-256, and both manifest digests. Each entry has\n10010|key/sequence, exact contract versions, strategies, fixture evidence, nullable\n10011|resume smoke, fidelity limits, validity, accepted/revoked status and reason/time.\n10012|Source entries are archive-only without smoke; target entries require current\n10013|passing fixtures and bounded resume smoke. Revocation and acceptance cannot\n10014|coexist.\n10015|\n10016|<code>SupportedEnvironmentTupleKey</code> contains exactly\n10017|<code>direction:source_read|target_write</code>,\n10018|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n10019|<code>candidate_kind:builtin|external</code>,\n10020|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n10021|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n10022|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>. The host constructs the\n10023|key from the adapter tuple and independently observed execution binding.\n10024|\n10025|The complete registry object contains exactly:\n10026|\n10027|| Member | Type and constraint |\n10028|| --- | --- |\n10029|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:supported-environment-tuples</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10030|| <code>registry_digest</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10031|| <code>registry_sequence</code> | uint53&gt;0 and strictly greater than every accepted predecessor |\n10032|| <code>ax_release</code> | Exact publishing/refreshing SemVer |\n10033|| <code>issued_at</code> / <code>not_before</code> / <code>not_after</code> | UTC timestamps; not-before no later than issued, not-after later than issued |\n10034|| <code>entries</code> | <code>SupportedEnvironmentTupleEntry[1..65536]</code>, sorted unique by JCS key bytes |\n10035|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys with no effect on identity, evidence, validity, admission, or revocation |\n10036|\n10037|<code>SupportedEnvironmentTupleEntry</code> contains exactly\n10038|<code>key:SupportedEnvironmentTupleKey</code>,\n10039|<code>entry_sequence:uint53&gt;0</code> no greater than registry sequence,\n10040|<code>contracts:SupportedContractVersions[1..64]</code> sorted unique by\n10041|contract ID, <code>strategies</code> as a sorted unique non-empty subset of the\n10042|five projection strategies, <code>fixture_evidence:FixtureEvidence</code>,\n10043|<code>resume_smoke_evidence:ResumeSmokeEvidence|null</code>,\n10044|<code>known_fidelity_limits:FidelityLimit[0..1024]</code> sorted unique by\n10045|code/class, <code>valid_from:timestamp</code>, <code>valid_until:timestamp</code>,\n10046|<code>status:accepted|revoked</code>,\n10047|<code>revocation_reason:string[1..4096]|null</code>,\n10048|<code>revoked_at:timestamp|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10049|\n10050|<code>SupportedContractVersions</code> contains exactly\n10051|<code>contract_id:string[1..256]</code> and\n10052|<code>versions:sorted unique SemVer[1..32]</code>. Allowed IDs are the\n10053|registered Provider Protocol, Session Adapter Protocol, Clone Raw/Capture/Bundle/\n10054|Projected/Read-Back manifests, Canonical Session/Event, Projection Plan,\n10055|Migration Checkpoint, Fidelity Report, Clone Validation Report,\n10056|Materialization Plan, Session Record/Event, Checkpoint, Transfer Manifest, and\n10057|Blob Descriptor identifiers. Wildcards, <code>latest</code>, empty, duplicated,\n10058|unknown, or unbounded versions are invalid.\n10059|\n10060|<code>FixtureEvidence</code> contains exactly\n10061|<code>suite_revision:string[1..128]</code>, <code>suite_digest:digest</code>,\n10062|<code>result=pass</code>, <code>executed_at:timestamp</code>,\n10063|<code>evidence_digest:digest</code>, and <code>fixture_count:uint53&gt;0</code>.\n10064|<code>ResumeSmokeEvidence</code> contains exactly <code>result=pass</code>,\n10065|<code>executed_at:timestamp</code>, <code>evidence_digest:digest</code>,\n10066|<code>native_cli_family:string[1..128]</code>, and\n10067|<code>bounded_continuation_turn_passed=true</code>.\n10068|<code>FidelityLimit</code> contains exactly <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n10069|<code>affected_class:string[1..128]</code>,\n10070|<code>maximum_disposition:fidelity-disposition</code>, and\n10071|<code>detail:string[1..4096]</code>.\n10072|\n10073|Source-read entries have exactly <code>strategies=[archive_only]</code> and null\n10074|resume evidence. Target-write entries exclude archive-only, require current\n10075|non-null passing resume evidence, and name only fixture-exercised strategies.\n10076|Accepted requires null revocation members and a current interval. Revoked\n10077|requires both revocation members; status is not part of the unique key, so\n10078|accepted and revoked rows cannot coexist.\n10079|\n10080|The JCS registry and detached SSHSIG are published at\n10081|<code>compatibility/supported-environment-tuples-v1.json</code> and\n10082|<code>compatibility/supported-environment-tuples-v1.json.sshsig</code> under\n10083|namespace <code>ax-supported-environment-tuples-v1</code> with the\n10084|release-pinned signer. Parsing, digest, signature, validity, ordering, and\n10085|monotonic sequence all fail closed. Failed/partial reads never mean absence.\n10086|Only AX release authority accepts or globally revokes; local policy may further\n10087|deny but cannot self-approve or override revocation.\n10088|\n10089|### 13.15 Directory continuation planning and execution\n10090|\n10091|The directory planner consumes one exact selected native instance, current AX\n10092|Session/lease/checkpoint/workspace facts when managed, authoritative lineage,\n10093|source/target reachability and Environment Tuples, target authentication\n10094|status, cloning fidelity estimate when applicable, operator intent, and policy.\n10095|It emits only the Section 10.8 Continuation Plan and\n10096|<code>planned_only</code>. Planning is read-only; it cannot quiesce, snapshot,\n10097|capture, transfer, materialize, adopt, allocate a provider transaction, launch,\n10098|attach, or change a lease.\n10099|\n10100|The shorthand <code>ax NAME</code> may execute without a separate confirmation\n10101|only when resolution yields exactly one safe non-mutating attach/resume route.\n10102|Takeover, fork, move, and every ambiguous route MUST remain a pure plan plus\n10103|confirmation; absent an interactive choice or exact non-interactive action the\n10104|result is <code>interactive_choice_required</code>. Route ranking MUST NOT turn\n10105|a mutating candidate into an implicit choice.\n10106|\n10107|The deterministic route matrix is:\n10108|\n10109|| Source/intent | Target | Eligible route and owner |\n10110|| --- | --- | --- |\n10111|| Managed running owner / attach | same host | <code>managed_local_attach</code>; existing AX terminal |\n10112|| Managed running owner / attach | another operator host, same owner | <code>managed_remote_attach</code>; authenticated AX attach |\n10113|| Managed stopped owner / resume | same host/environment | <code>managed_local_resume</code>; Provider 2 plus winning AX lease |\n10114|| Managed / takeover | different host, same environment | <code>managed_takeover</code>; Sections 13.6/13.7 and workspace cohort |\n10115|| Managed / fork | any eligible AX host | <code>managed_fork</code>; Section 13.8 |\n10116|| Unmanaged exact instance / adopt | owning host only | <code>adopt_existing_native</code>; gated transaction below |\n10117|| Managed or unmanaged / clone | same environment | <code>same_environment_clone</code>; safe native fast path or v0.3 canonical pipeline |\n10118|| Managed or unmanaged / clone | different environment | <code>cross_environment_clone</code>; Section 13.14 plus AX transfer/launch |\n10119|| Managed / move | different environment | <code>cross_environment_move</code>; clone target first, then fenced source release |\n10120|| Unmanaged / open | owning host only | <code>open_unmanaged_local</code>; explicit absence of AX guarantees |\n10121|| Any / unsupported tuple | no native target | <code>archive_or_context_fallback</code>; never reported as clone |\n10122|\n10123|An unmanaged instance on another host can only be adopted by its source node or\n10124|cloned into a managed target. Workspace transfer precedes session\n10125|materialization when required. Shared Workspace Groups obey the existing whole-\n10126|cohort/separate-worktree rules; the directory cannot invent another workspace\n10127|copy mode.\n10128|\n10129|A direct unmanaged move is unavailable. An unmanaged source has no AX Session,\n(more lines below)"}}}
