de> | diagnostic timestamp and reverse-DNS object |\n6271|\n6272|The initial mapping is exactly <code>claude-code -> claude</code> and\n6273|<code>codex -> codex</code>. Future mappings are signed manifest/registry data.\n6274|Environment Observation reuses the Section 13.14 Environment Tuple admission\n6275|model and does not create a second capability authority.\n6276|\n6277|Native Session Observation contains exactly:\n6278|\n6279|| Member | Type/constraint |\n6280|| --- | --- |\n6281|| identity | exact schema/version plus <code>observation_id:digest</code> |\n6282|| source | <code>instance_id:digest</code>, <code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>installation_id:digest</code> |\n6283|| chain | <code>observation_sequence:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>previous_observation_id:digest|null</code> |\n6284|| management | <code>managed_session_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest|null</code>, <code>lineage_anchor_hint:UUIDv7|digest|null</code> |\n6285|| head | <code>source_generation:string[1..512]|null</code>, <code>head_digest:digest|null</code> |\n6286|| identity/state | <code>identity_confidence:exact|strong|weak</code>, <code>presence:present|missing|unknown</code>, <code>native_state:active|idle|waiting|stopped|failed|unknown</code>, <code>resumability:validated|likely|unavailable|unknown</code> |\n6287|| workspace/title | <code>workspace_identity:WorkspaceIdentity|null</code>, <code>provider_title:string[1..512]|null</code> |\n6288|| diagnostics | <code>created_at:timestamp|null</code>, <code>updated_at:timestamp|null</code>, <code>message_counts:MessageCounts</code>, <code>preview_status:current|stale|unavailable|policy_blocked</code>, <code>warnings:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>, <code>observed_at:timestamp</code>, <code>extensions</code> |\n6289|\n6290|<code>WorkspaceIdentity</code> contains exactly\n6291|<code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>,\n6292|<code>repository_identity:string[1..256]|null</code>,\n6293|<code>workspace_digest:digest|null</code>, and <code>branch:string[1..256]|null</code>;\n6294|it contains no absolute path. <code>MessageCounts</code> contains exactly\n6295|<code>user:uint53|null</code> and <code>assistant:uint53|null</code>. A managed\n6296|observation requires exact Provider Identity evidence; workspace, title,\n6297|process, timestamp, or text matches are insufficient. Weak identity cannot\n6298|authorize remote continuation or lineage.\n6299|\n6300|Inventory Batch contains exactly <code>schema</code>,\n6301|<code>schema_version</code>, <code>batch_id:digest</code>,\n6302|<code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>batch_sequence:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n6303|<code>previous_batch_id:digest|null</code>,\n6304|<code>cursor_before:string[0..4096]|null</code>,\n6305|<code>cursor_after:string[0..4096]|null</code>,\n6306|<code>environment_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code>,\n6307|<code>native_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536]</code>,\n6308|<code>scan_root_authority_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code>,\n6309|<code>adapter_builds:sorted unique AdapterBuild[1..256]</code>,\n6310|<code>started_at:timestamp</code>, <code>completed_at:timestamp</code>,\n6311|<code>partial:boolean</code>, <code>error_codes:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>,\n6312|and <code>extensions</code>. <code>AdapterBuild</code> contains exactly\n6313|<code>environment_id</code>, <code>adapter_version</code>, and\n6314|<code>executable_sha256</code>.\n6315|\n6316|Only a successful non-partial batch for the same root authority and realm may\n6317|publish <code>presence=missing</code>. Failed/offline/partial scans preserve the\n6318|prior presence and change freshness, not existence. For one source instance,\n6319|the current observation is the valid contiguous chain head with greatest\n6320|sequence. A same-sequence branch is <code>observation_conflict</code>; a gap\n6321|quarantines later observations until the missing predecessor or a signed\n6322|source recovery root arrives. Timestamps never order the chain.\n6323|\n6324|A <code>missing</code> instance remains browseable and searchable in Version 1.\n6325|Display policy MAY hide it behind an explicit missing/archive filter, but no\n6326|scan result automatically emits an AX tombstone, deletes an observation or\n6327|annotation, or removes the entry from the catalog. Retention and an explicit\n6328|future deletion contract, not absence inference, own removal.\n6329|\n6330|#### 10.8.2 Conversation Lineage and annotations\n6331|\n6332|Conversation Lineage is a derived graph whose nodes are AX Session IDs and\n6333|unmanaged instance IDs. Authoritative edges are exactly <code>ax_fork</code>,\n6334|<code>session_clone</code>, <code>cross_environment_move</code>,\n(more lines below)"}}}
