{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a073c4-c6ec-7382-9783-190de4ee11a6"},"sequence":580,"recorded_at":1780531400001155,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"f296fe6d-722f-4e1a-907d-4fb2554f7e2b"},"task_id":"f296fe6d-722f-4e1a-907d-4fb2554f7e2b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"f296fe6d-722f-4e1a-907d-4fb2554f7e2b","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/provhost/closed_vocabulary_census_test.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"go/ast\"\n5|\t\"go/parser\"\n6|\t\"go/token\"\n7|\t\"os\"\n8|\t\"path/filepath\"\n9|\t\"reflect\"\n10|\t\"sort\"\n11|\t\"strings\"\n12|\t\"testing\"\n13|\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n15|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/specdoc\"\n16|)\n17|\n18|// This file closes the closed-vocabulary class for the shapes the\n19|// census derives: every package-level []string, map[string]bool, and\n20|// map[string]string consulted by a membership check carries a\n21|// registered spec derivation that executes. The eight enum\n22|// derivations in closed_vocabularies_test.go are hand-registered one\n23|// by one, and nine more membership-checked vocabularies existed in\n24|// production with no derivation at all: a widened member set still\n25|// admitted its extra body with the suite green. Enumerating one more\n26|// hand-written list per vocabulary would move the gap, not close it,\n27|// so the domain is derived the way\n28|// TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed already does for refusal\n29|// arms: deriveMembershipVocabularies parses production source for\n30|// the three package-level shapes, and\n31|// TestClosedVocabularyCensusCoversEveryMembershipVocabulary requires\n32|// each to carry a registered spec derivation. A new vocabulary with\n33|// no derivation fails here instead of passing silently.\n34|//\n35|// Three vocabularies used to live outside the derived shapes as\n36|// switch statements (the response envelope member set, the execution\n37|// profile set, the transaction state set); a widened case admitted\n38|// its extra value with the suite green. They are package-level maps\n39|// now (responseMembers, profileNames, statusStates), so the census\n40|// derives them like the rest. The remaining switch in production\n41|// dispatches on an already-validated state rather than admitting\n42|// members, and TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified pins that:\n43|// any new switch must be classified before the suite passes.\n44|//\n45|// A membership check is one of: an unknownMember argument, a direct\n46|// map index, or a range that builds an allow-set or compares\n47|// element-wise. The *Required order lists are deliberately out of\n48|// scope: their only production use is as missingMember arguments,\n49|// they encode deterministic refusal order rather than containment,\n50|// and dropping their last entry is behaviour-preserving (the omitted\n51|// body still refuses). profileProviders is likewise out of scope:\n52|// nothing in production consults it. The []Operation registries are\n53|// out of scope by type and stay derived by\n54|// TestOperationRegistryIsDerivedFromSpec. Function-local literals\n55|// (such as the required list inside checkResponseMembers) belong to\n56|// the *Required order-list class above, not to containment. An empty\n57|// derivation — zero files scanned, zero vocabularies found, a spec\n58|// window with no members — fails closed rather than measuring\n59|// nothing.\n60|\n61|// requireMemberSet asserts the production member set holds exactly\n62|// the spec-derived members, order-insensitive: maps carry no order.\n63|// Either side empty is a blind check, so both fail outright.\n64|func requireMemberSet(t *testing.T, name string, got, want []string) {\n65|\tt.Helper()\n66|\tif len(got) == 0 {\n67|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s holds no members; the check is blind\", name)\n68|\t}\n69|\tif len(want) == 0 {\n70|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s derives no members from the pinned document; the check is blind\", name)\n71|\t}\n72|\tordered := func(members []string) []string {\n73|\t\tduplicated := append([]string(nil), members...)\n74|\t\tsort.Strings(duplicated)\n75|\t\treturn duplicated\n76|\t}\n77|\tif !reflect.DeepEqual(ordered(got), ordered(want)) {\n78|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s = %v, want the pinned member set %v\", name, ordered(got), ordered(want))\n79|\t}\n80|\tt.Logf(\"%s coverage: %d/%d members derived\", name, len(got), len(want))\n81|}\n82|\n83|// exampleObjectKeysOf parses the top-level keys of the JSON example\n84|// embedded in a spec window, in document order. A window with no\n85|// JSON object is a blind check, so it fails outright.\n86|func exampleObjectKeysOf(t *testing.T, window string) []string {\n87|\tt.Helper()\n88|\tstart := strings.Index(window, \"{\")\n89|\tend := strings.LastIndex(window, \"}\")\n90|\tif start < 0 || end <= start {\n91|\t\tt.Fatal(\"spec window holds no JSON object; the check is blind\")\n92|\t}\n93|\texample, fault := decodeStrictObject([]byte(window[start : end+1]))\n94|\tif fault != nil {\n95|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"spec example is not a strict object: %v %q\", fault.detail, fault.member)\n96|\t}\n97|\tvar keys []string\n98|\tfor key := range example {\n99|\t\tkeys = append(keys, key)\n100|\t}\n(more lines below)"}}}
