{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000eccf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a073c4-c6ec-7382-9783-190de4ee11a6"},"sequence":5314,"recorded_at":1780531400010623,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"5121b34e-979a-4f09-b2a9-ee98e90b0904"},"task_id":"5121b34e-979a-4f09-b2a9-ee98e90b0904","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"5121b34e-979a-4f09-b2a9-ee98e90b0904","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-169-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"The request envelope contains exactly\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.md | head -3 | cut -c1-100; echo ===; sed -n '2860,2875p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.md | cut -c1-160; echo ===; grep -n \\\"| <code>probe</code> |\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.md | head -5; echo ===; sed -n '3596,3626p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.md | cut -c1-130\",\n  \"description\": \"Show envelope, capability, probe, manifest raws\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"2686:The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\\n3497:The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\\n3738:The request envelope contains exactly <code>schema</code>,\\n===\\nThe probe object is closed and every displayed member is required.\\n<code>provider_version</code> is a 1–128 character exact version string,\\narchitecture is <code>amd64</code> or <code>arm64</code>, and\\n<code>capabilities</code> contains exactly the seven requested registry keys.\\nEach capability value contains exactly <code>status</code>,\\n<code>enabled</code>, <code>evidence</code>, and a 0–2,048 character\\n<code>detail</code>. <code>warnings</code> is a sorted, unique array of at most\\n1,024 strings of at most 2,048 characters each.\\n\\nStatus is one of <code>available</code>, <code>conditional</code>,\\n<code>unsupported</code>, or <code>unknown</code>. Only\\n<code>available</code> MAY set <code>enabled</code> true. Evidence is one of\\n<code>documented</code>, <code>probed</code>, <code>accepted_test</code>,\\n<code>provider_contract</code>, <code>inferred</code>,\\n<code>acceptance_required</code>, or <code>none</code>.\\n\\n===\\n1132:| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\\\|linux\\\\|wsl2\\\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\\n1167:| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\\n3073:| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, requested_capabilities:sorted unique capability-name[0..7]}</code> | Provider Probe object (Section 7.4) |\\n3583:| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\\n3789:| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\\\|linux\\\\|wsl2\\\\|windows,architecture:amd64\\\\|arm64,requested_environment_ids:sorted unique environment-id[0..64],requested_capabilities:sorted unique directory-capability[0..8],extensions}</code> | <code>{host_id:UUIDv7,node_build:DirectoryNodeBuild,policy_digest:digest,environments:EnvironmentObservation[0..256],findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code> | none |\\n===\\n\\nCandidate objects are addressed only by their exact\\n<code>*_candidate_id</code> in the request's fresh sink. The core retrieves,\\nvalidates, rehashes, and seals them. A partial, malformed, over-limit, escaped,\\nor authority-unresolvable result is an error, never an empty or absent result\\nand never fallback permission.\\n\\nSession Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly:\\n\\n| Member | Type and constraint |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</cod\\n| <code>provider_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>; equal to Provider Manifest and discovered candidate ID |\\n| <code>environment_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}</code>; one semantic native environment |\\n| <code>display_name</code> / <code>adapter_version</code> | UTF-8 string[1..128] / SemVer |\\n| <code>environment_version_range</code> | Non-empty constraint string[1..256] |\\n| <code>platforms</code> | Sorted unique non-empty subset of <code>linux&#124;macos&#124;windows&#124;wsl2</code> |\\n| <code>operations</code> / <code>capability_names</code> | Complete ordered registries in this section, no omissions or duplicate\\n| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; cannot add operations, capabilities, or trust facts |\\n\\nIts host-computed JCS SHA-256 is\\n<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest</code> and is not embedded.\\n\\nSession Adapter Probe 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly\\n<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-probe</code>,\\n<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>, <code>provider_id</code>,\\n<code>adapter_manifest_digest</code>, <code>adapter_version</code>,\\n<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</c