{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000f84d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a073c4-c6ec-7382-9783-190de4ee11a6"},"sequence":6785,"recorded_at":1780531400013565,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a60ea177-b824-4d2f-9417-732f60b58837"},"task_id":"a60ea177-b824-4d2f-9417-732f60b58837","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a60ea177-b824-4d2f-9417-732f60b58837","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-232-1\",\n  \"command\": \"tail -40 LOGBOOK.md; echo ===; grep -c \\\"\\\" LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Show LOGBOOK tail and format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"- FIX (G3): new internal `TestReplicationMembersAreExactlyTheClosedTable` pins the live `replicationMembers` map in both directions plus the size (64 members). C40c (add) and C40-init-injection red there; C40b/C40d red there and at the entry. External test comment restated to its half (want subset production) with the reverse cited.\\n- FIX (G4): new `TestDerivedVocabulariesAreExactlyTheAdmittedSets` derives all four parser vocabularies (states, operations, effects, transports) from switch-case lists resolved through string consts, both directions plus size, and pins `conformanceOperations` to the derived operation set — the \\\"pinned by\\\" citation now holds. Refused samples restated as sampling bounds over the unbounded string domain and extended with the reviewer's exact survivor strings (`detached`, `detach`, `input_reopened`, `ssh_tunnel`), each now behaviorally refused.\\n- BOUNDS (recorded, not closed): W11 (DigestFile allowlist is function-wide, no detail pin), W13 (bespoke error types outside both spellings), mismatchf format-verb interpolation (derivation now fatals on any constructor call without exactly one string-literal argument — zero such sites today; vet catches non-constant formats). P11 stale bound dropped (C20 killed); P13 declined closure stands.\\n- TOOLING: round-3 runner (`.temp/TASK-260830-1snnef-r2/probe.py` family successor `.temp/TASK-260830-1snnef-r3/probe3.py`) snapshots and hash-verifies every touched file regardless of extension, with a JSON-restore self-test and a porcelain+fingerprint tree-identity check — a T01-shaped JSON mutation can no longer contaminate the tree.\\n- EVIDENCE: 21/21 replayed red, 0 survived, 0 anchor-missing (G1x6 incl. control, G2x5 incl. control and unused-var, G3x4 incl. init injection and both reclassifications, G4x5 incl. control, F2 guard). Tree verified identical before/after (porcelain + watched hashes).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/conformance_test.go` (G1/G3-comment/G4), `internal_pin_test.go` (G3 pin), `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (G2 twin + single-arg assertion + bounds), `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry + P11 correction). No production change, no arm-table change, 193/193 undisturbed.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, `clauses_discharged=17/403`). Package coverage 90.0% statements. Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef round-3 rework: unpinned legacyForward closed by a white-box pin, plus a correction\\n- CORRECTION: the round-1 and round-2 entries above claim C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\\\"screen\\\"`) is killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair` and drop the P11 bound on that basis. That claim is false, and the error is the reviewer's (round-2 verdict), not the producer's — the rework followed the verdict. C20 lands on `BuiltinTmux` while `ProjectToLegacy` iterates a map, so the kill was a coin flip over iteration order: 5 red and 7 green across 12 runs of the reviewer's own probe. A single red on a map-iteration mutant proves nothing. LESSON, applied to every mutant below: a mutant over map iteration (or anything else iterating a map, e.g. `ProjectToLegacy`) is run repeatedly before its verdict is believed.\\n- FIX (H1, blocking): new white-box `TestLegacyForwardIsExactlyTheImmutablePair` (`internal_pin_test.go`) holds the live `legacyForward` map to exactly `{tmux, conpty}` in both directions plus the size — the `replicationMembers` idiom from this same CR — and additionally pins injectivity (distinct canonical values), which `ProjectToLegacy`'s documented determinism rested on unenforced. The black-box forward comment is restated to its half (sampling bound, not closure) with the reverse cited, and the reviewer's escape strings join the refused samples (`TranslateLegacyBackend(\\\"screen\\\")`, `ProjectToLegacy(\\\"vendor.screen\\\")`).\\n- FIX (H2, bound, closed cheaply): new `rejectPlainErrorAliases` fails the suite on any `errors.New`/`fmt.Errorf`-kin reference outside direct-call position, in every function including the two allowlisted ones (an alias inside `validatePlatforms` would bypass the funneled detail pin). Stated bounds and the allowlist test comment record the closure. Bespoke error types outside both spellings remain the disclosed bound.\\n- EVIDENCE: L3 (`\\\"screen\\\": \\\"vendor.screen\\\"`) 12/12 red, C20 (`\\\"screen\\\": BuiltinTmux`) 12/12 red, each over `-run TestLegacy|TestHistorical`; the new pin alone red on C20 with the size message (`holds 3 names, want exactly 2`); H2 alias (`var newPlain = errors.New` + call from a FuncDecl) 3/3 red on `TestPlainErrors`. Tree verified identical before/after (file-content compare + restore assert).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/internal_pin_test.go` (H1 pin), `conformance_test.go` (H1 comment + 2 samples), `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (H2 alias gate + bounds), `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). No production change, no arm-table change, 193/193 undisturbed.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, `clauses_discharged=17/403`). Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\\n### 2321 — A local copy of a shared gate needs a pin, not a comment; a registry that only counts itself cannot see new code\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B3): `provhost.decodeStrictObject` re-implemented strict decoding without the shared `canonicaljson` surrogate rule, and Go's `encoding/json` replaces a lone `\\\\ud800` escape with U+FFFD silently — so Section 1.6 wire bodies carrying lone surrogates were admitted. Same class as the sibling story's decoder gap.\\n- FIX: local `hasLoneSurrogateEscape` gate in `internal/provhost/surrogate.go` (local copy because `canonicaljson` is frozen across both unlanded stories), called first from `decodeStrictObject`; one `\\\\ud800` fixture per production entry plus `TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON`, a 13-vector pin driving both the local gate and `canonicaljson.Canonicalize` so the copies cannot drift.\\n- ANOMALY: the first gate version used `switch` and reddened `TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified` — the package census bans switches as membership-gate hiding spots. Rewritten with if/else, identical verdicts, green. A gate's own residue rules apply to the fix too.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B4): `tracecheck` verifies registry -> code only, so ~3,700 lines of `internal/provider` + `internal/provhost` landed with the gate green under gap prose asserting \\\"no provider manifest is implemented anywhere\\\". The census enumerates what registered itself.\\n- FIX: 4 acceptance cases + 4 section bindings (7.1, 7.6, 7.7, 8), 4 gap rewrites (5.5, 7.2, 7.3, 7.5), re-pinned hash; report now bindings=53 unevidenced=45 clauses 17/428. Reverse scan (every `internal/*` package owned or explicitly excluded) recorded as open work, not implemented here.\\n- DECISION (A2/A3/A4, recorded in code): CheckIdentity duplication is deliberate (different error surface, shared package frozen); Provider Protocol 3.0.0 is a stated non-owner bound, not a defect; provider's cause-appending errors must be rebuilt, not quoted, at the future cmd/ax lift (`refuseCausalLeak`).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/surrogate*.go`, `protocol.go`, refusal inventory (floor 162->164), `profile_test.go` (cross-plane set test), `identity.go`/`doc.go` bounds, `internal/provider/doc.go` composition contract, ownership registry + pin + report/golden/README figures.\\n- STATUS: Resolved. `go test ./...` and `-cover` green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, admit-all and narrowing mutants red as required. TASK-260830-32jeti round-4, handed to review.\\n\\n### 1244 — A deadline borrowed from pipe ownership is not a deadline; a shared hand list is not a pin\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F1): the `os.Pipe` rewrite in `internal/provhost/runner.go` fixed the Wait-closes-StdoutPipe race but removed the only thing that unblocked the post-Wait drain. `exec.WaitDelay` closes pipes exec itself owns; with caller-supplied `*os.File` pipes nothing closes them, so `readCapped` waits for EOF until every writer is gone and a setsid-detached grandchild holds `Host.Call` open for its whole lifetime (measured 20.3-20.7s against sleep 20, frame accepted with err=nil).\\n- FIX: the waiter owns the bound now — `command.Wait()` runs in a goroutine under `select` on the call context, both drains collect through `collectDrains` under the same context, and closing the read ends fails blocked drains at once. A `Process.Kill` backstop covers a self-detached direct child, which the group-aimed `Cancel` misses. The round-6 EPIPE rule is untouched: with the wait reaped and stdout holding a frame, the frame still governs.\\n- ANOMALY: the first regression probe passed vacuously in 0.79s — python3 cold start under load can exceed the 400ms deadline kill, so no grandchild ever existed to hold the pipe. A hang test whose fixture loses a startup race proves nothing. Rebuilt on perl (millisecond start) with the kill seconds away; 3/3 red at the sleeper lifetime before the fix, green at the deadline after.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F2): the 13-vector corpus was literal-versus-literal — both implementations matched the same hand list, so a narrowed low-surrogate ceiling (SG1, 1023 admitted) and a narrowed uppercase hex range (SG5, 473 admitted) survived 6/6. Raw WTF-8 (`\\\\xed\\\\xa0\\\\x80`) arrived through an encoding the escape scanner never sees and became U+FFFD silently.\\n- FIX: `decodeStrictObject` refuses non-UTF-8 first (mirroring `canonicaljson.decodeStrict` order), and the corpus is replaced by a 239,630-vector derived sweep — full BMP x hex case, surrogate x 16 case mixes, high x boundary/non-low seconds, sampled positions plus all-surrogate member names, full BMP raw (WTF-8 form for surrogates), malformed patterns, astral samples — every verdict judged by the independent implementation. SG1 diverges on 19,482 vectors, SG5 on 4,411; gate removal reddens the identity row with err=nil and the sweep on 2,059.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F3): `checkResponseMembers` ran before the version gate, so only a v2-shaped 3.x envelope reached `incompatible_protocol`; the tree's own pinned 7.2 quote scopes that member rule to major 2. Fixed the ordering, not the doc: a `foreignMajor` peek (protocol identity plus readable foreign version, trusts nothing, refuses nothing) skips the v2 `ok`/member rules so the single existing mismatch site decides. No new refusal arm; floor untouched by F3.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/runner.go`, `protocol.go`, `surrogate*.go`, `identity.go` + comment corrections, `runner_test.go`, `protocol_test.go`, `identity_test.go`, refusal inventory (floor 164->166: one UTF-8 frame arm plus its status-body expansion, each witnessed).\\n- STATUS: Resolved. Build, vet, GOOS=windows vet, gofmt clean; `go test ./...` 15/15 green; provhost `-race` green; provhost 85.8%, provider 97.0%. TASK-260830-32jeti round-8, handed to review.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-32jeti: two green branches, one red combination — syscall.Mkfifo under GOOS=windows vet\\n- FINDING: the new CI step `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` failed on the merged tree with `terminalbackend_test.go:972:20: undefined: syscall.Mkfifo` — the only failure across all 16 packages. Invisible on both parents by construction: the story branch added the gate before the package existed (nothing to compile, exit 0), and trunk added the `syscall.Mkfifo` FIFO case without the gate (never compiled under Windows). Each branch was green on its own; only the combination is red. A per-branch gate that never meets the code it must check proves nothing about the merge.\\n- FIX: moved only the FIFO case out of `TestDigestFile` into `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` in new `internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend_unix_test.go`, following the `internal/localstore/projection_unix_test.go` pattern. Correction worth recording: the `_unix` filename suffix alone constrains nothing (`unix` is a build tag, not a GOOS value, so the suffix form matches no `_GOOS` pattern) — the first attempt with suffix-only still failed windows vet, and the explicit `//go:build unix` line is what excludes Windows. The shared test file drops the `syscall` import and keeps a pointer comment; no other Go file touched.\\n- EVIDENCE: `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 16/16 green with `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` observed PASS on linux (a moved test that stops executing is not a fix), `tracecheck` exit 0. TASK-260830-32jeti, handed to review.\\n===\\n899\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 12677,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3170,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
