{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000f873","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a073c4-c6ec-7382-9783-190de4ee11a6"},"sequence":6804,"recorded_at":1780531400013603,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"eb096e1e-33cc-4e91-a590-1b531924cfec"},"task_id":"eb096e1e-33cc-4e91-a590-1b531924cfec","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"eb096e1e-33cc-4e91-a590-1b531924cfec","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-233-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat >> LOGBOOK.md <<'EOF'\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0: sessadapter closed-vocabulary census derived from the pinned document, vocab gates looped, acceptance cases registered\\n- FIX: `census_test.go` used `specdoc` without deriving from it (vet failure on the unused import). Added `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec` (20 closed bodies: every Required list in document order plus the Members map as a set, with the success/failure envelopes derived by the spec's own first-four-fields rule, the manifest from its table's first-column spans, and the doctor result from the operation table) and `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec` (16 vocabularies pinned to their spec unions; operation/capability registries in order, value sets as sets).\\n- FINDINGS (all verified against the raw document, each would have been a silent wrong-source derivation): the request envelope sentence exists three times (7.5-style, 7.8, 7.9) and the capability-value sentence twice (Provider Probe 7.4 vs Session Adapter Probe 7.8) — selection is by a structural fragment only the Session Adapter sentence carries, and the parse still covers the whole sentence; member sentences contain digit-period-digit abbreviations (`Section 7.5`, `Structured Error 1.1`), so the sentence scanner skips those; unions use three pipe encodings (`\\\\|` in the operation table, raw `|` in prose, `&#124;` in the manifest table); the manifest table pairs members per row (`schema`/`schema_version` etc.), so the first cell contributes every bare snake_case span; the `probe` row name recurs in four tables, so row unions are windowed to the 7.8 registry table; fidelity profiles come from the `projection-plan` operation row (4 values — the 13.14 `Profiles are` sentence lists 5 including `archive_only`, which is a strategy there, never a profile).\\n- REFACTOR (production-first, same `var` + `validX` loop idiom the package already uses): `capabilityStatuses`/`validCapabilityStatus` (probe.go), `readPurposes`/`validReadPurpose` and `findingSeverities`/`validFindingSeverity` (context.go), `tupleArchitectures`/`validTupleArchitecture` (tuple.go); the four inline-literal checks now loop the tables. Roles, directions, candidate kinds, and platforms derive from the existing `Role`/`Direction`/`CandidateKind`/`scalar.Platform` consts with no production change (tuple platforms delegate to `scalar.ParsePlatform`).\\n- TEST: new `TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status` — no behavioral test refused a fifth status, so a `return true` mutant of `validCapabilityStatus` survived the suite with the static census green. The mutant is now killed by the entry point (`DecodeProbe`).\\n- EVIDENCE (executed mutants, `/tmp/sessadapter-mutants.sh`, tree verified identical before/after): M1 `capabilityStatuses`+`bogus` killed by `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec`; M2 `findingSeverities`+`fatal` killed by `TestDecodeFindingRules/bad_severity`; M3 `requestMembers`+`zzz` killed by `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec/request_envelope`; M4 `validCapabilityStatus`→`return true` (all searched-for tokens preserved) leaves the static census green and is killed by the behavioral suite (`TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status`); M5 unregistered vocabulary-shaped `var` killed by `TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered`. 8/8 as required, 0 survived.\\n- TRACEABILITY: 7 acceptance cases appended (`session-adapter-discovery/-manifest/-probe/-operations/-limits/-idempotency/-tuple-gates`, each bound to one production declaration and its named positive/refusal tests), digest re-pinned to `78d9bc9b...`, count pins 81->88, README ownership paragraph 81->88 plus a sessadapter disclosure paragraph that keeps the Section 7.8 clause-level binding `unevidenced` (no clause enumerated — no clause-level claim made).\\n- NOTE (pre-existing, not touched): README still says \\\"One admitted binding out of forty-nine\\\" while `tracecheck` measures `bindings=53` — stale since before this task (first run here already showed 53). Flagged for the review rather than fixed in passing.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/sessadapter/{census_test,probe,context,tuple}.go` + `probe_test.go` (bad status), `internal/traceability/{ownership.v0.5.0.json,traceability.go,traceability_test.go,cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go}`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). Work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\nEOF\\necho APPENDED\",\n  \"description\": \"Append LOGBOOK entry\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"APPENDED\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
