{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000fb2f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a073c4-c6ec-7382-9783-190de4ee11a6"},"sequence":7154,"recorded_at":1780531400014303,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5409c77-5362-4816-80c2-4a2c06765e09"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Done. TASK-260830-2z3se0 work is complete in the worktree, uncommitted, with board evidence attached. Status left at `development` — review/landing is the orchestrator's step.\n\nWhat this turn did, on top of the package built earlier in the task:\n\n- Closed the red suite: `census_test.go` now derives from `specdoc` instead of merely importing it — `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec` pins 20 closed bodies (order + set) and `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec` pins 16 vocabularies against their spec unions.\n- Production refactor in the package's existing `var` + `validX` loop idiom: `capabilityStatuses`, `readPurposes`, `findingSeverities`, `tupleArchitectures` now back their gates; roles/directions/kinds/platforms derive from existing consts.\n- Added `TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status`: no behavioral test refused a fifth status, so a token-preserving `return true` mutant survived — now killed at the `DecodeProbe` entry point.\n- Traceability: 7 `session-adapter-*` acceptance cases registered, digest re-pinned (`78d9bc9b…`), counts 81→88, README updated with counts plus a sessadapter paragraph that keeps the 7.8 clause binding `unevidenced`.\n- LOGBOOK entry appended; `TASK-260830-2z3se0/verification-evidence.log` attached; all 13 checklist items checked with the AC ratio in notes: **10 of 10 rows** (9 driven through named entry-point tests, crash-evidence N/A by the stated no-durable-state bound).\n\nObserved verification: `go test ./...` 17/17 green, `-race` and 81.1% cover on sessadapter, `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` + `gofmt` clean, `tracecheck` ok (88 cases), 8/8 narrowing mutants killed with the tree verified identical before/after. Two flags for review: README's \"forty-nine bindings\" prose was already stale (measures 53) before this task — left untouched; and \"lint clean\" rests on vet+gofmt since no linter is configured.","reason":null}}
